# Append-only doc ledgers: union merge auto-concatenates both sides on conflict.
# Safe iff the file is strictly append-only-at-EOF (no post-write edits to existing entries).
# Trade-off: silent duplicate KN-N / DE-N IDs if both branches allocate the same number
# (renumbering already deferred separately, not a regression).
docs/pending.md     merge=union
docs/knowledge.md   merge=union
docs/decisions.md   merge=union
docs/completed.md   merge=union
.bkit/friction.md merge=union

# Append-only NDJSON workflow status logs: union auto-concatenates both branches'
# appended lines server-side so a per-FID status log never blocks a merge.
# Safe iff strictly append-only (prior lines never mutated); the reader folds + dedupes
# by (workflow, step, parentSha, at) and orders by `at`, tolerating interleave/duplication.
# Scoped to bkit's status files only — NOT a blanket *.jsonl (union would corrupt a
# consumer's non-append-only .jsonl data on merge).
docs/plans/**/status.jsonl merge=union

# <!-- bkit:end -->
